---
layout: net-layout.njk
title: UGC NET English PYQs
eleventyComputed:
  description: "Take real UGC-NET English papers from earlier years as an online test, with a clock and a full answer review. Most papers are free, and some need {% if paidLayer.live %}the All Access pass{% else %}a free login{% endif %}."
crumb_label: English PYQs
eyebrow: Previous-year question papers
---
{# CLAUDE.md rule 18. The cards come from _data/netPyqs.json (grouped by year in _data/netPyqYears.js). A new paper is one
   registry line plus its question file; this page needs no change. A LOGIN paper (access: "login") has no file: its card
   shows the padlock to a guest and Start to a student, or "Coming soon" until it is Live, and assets/net-pyq-live.js flips
   it from the live paper catalog with no rebuild (rule 17). #}
<section class="net-pyq" aria-labelledby="net-pyq-title">
  <header class="net-pyq-intro">
    <div>
      <h2 id="net-pyq-title">Choose a paper</h2>
      <p>Each paper opens as a real test, with one question at a time, a clock and a full review at the end. Most papers are free for everyone. {% if paidLayer.live %}A paper marked with a padlock needs the <a href="/pass/">All Access pass</a>.{% else %}A paper marked with a padlock needs a free login.{% endif %}</p>
    </div>
    <span class="net-pyq-total">{{ netPyqPapers.length }} paper{% if netPyqPapers.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
  </header>

  <div class="net-pyq-years">
    {# Every year group is open by default so no paper is hidden on this reference page (owner, 2026-11-18:
       2012 stays on top, newer years below). The reader can still collapse a year with the summary. #}
    {% for group in netPyqYears %}
    <details class="net-pyq-year" open>
      <summary>
        <span class="net-pyq-year-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="net-pyq-year-name">{{ group.year }}</span>
        <small>{{ group.papers.length }} paper{% if group.papers.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</small>
        <img class="net-pyq-chevron" src="/assets/icons/feather/chevron-down.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22">
      </summary>
      <div class="net-pyq-sections">
      {% for section in group.sections %}
      <section class="net-pyq-section" aria-labelledby="net-pyq-{{ group.year }}-{{ section.paper | lower }}">
        <header class="net-pyq-section-head">
          <h3 id="net-pyq-{{ group.year }}-{{ section.paper | lower }}">Paper {{ section.paper }}</h3>
          <small>{{ section.papers.length }} paper{% if section.papers.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}, oldest first</small>
        </header>
        <ol class="net-pyq-grid">
          {% for paper in section.papers %}
          <li>
            {%- if paper.access == "login" %}
            <div class="net-pyq-card net-pyq-card-login" data-net-pyq-slot="{{ paper.setId }}" data-slot-state="{{ 'live' if paper.live else 'soon' }}" aria-label="{{ paper.title }}">
              <span class="net-pyq-step" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index }}</span>
              <span class="net-pyq-card-copy">
                <strong>{{ paper.session }}{% if paper.shift %} · {{ paper.shift }}{% endif %}</strong>
                <span>Paper {{ paper.paper }} · <span data-pyq-count>{{ paper.count }} questions</span> · {% if paidLayer.live %}Needs the All Access pass{% else %}Needs a free login{% endif %}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="net-pyq-actions" data-slot-live{% if not paper.live %} hidden{% endif %}>
                <a class="net-pyq-go net-pyq-go-lock" data-guest-only hidden href="/login/?next={{ paper.href | urlencode }}" aria-label="{{ paper.title }} needs a login. Log in to open it." title="Log in to open {{ paper.title }}"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="2" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
                <a class="net-pyq-go" data-auth-only hidden href="{{ paper.href }}" aria-label="Start {{ paper.title }}">Start</a>
              </span>
              <span class="net-pyq-soon" data-slot-soon{% if paper.live %} hidden{% endif %}>Coming soon</span>
            </div>
            {%- else %}
            <a class="net-pyq-card" href="{{ paper.href }}" aria-label="Start {{ paper.title }}">
              <span class="net-pyq-step" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index }}</span>
              <span class="net-pyq-card-copy">
                <strong>{{ paper.session }}{% if paper.shift %} · {{ paper.shift }}{% endif %}</strong>
                <span>Paper {{ paper.paper }} · {{ paper.count }} questions · Free · No login</span>
              </span>
              <span class="net-pyq-go" aria-hidden="true">Start</span>
            </a>
            {%- endif %}
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </section>
      {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="net-reading net-pyq-note" aria-labelledby="net-pyq-note-title">
  <h2 id="net-pyq-note-title">How these papers are marked</h2>
  <p>The questions and answers follow the UGC question paper and its updated answer key. This site counts one right answer for each question. Sometimes the official key accepts more than one option, or gives marks to every candidate. In that case the test counts one option, and the explanation for that question tells you which one.</p>
  <p>On a free paper, your answers stay in this browser. Log in if you also want your results kept with your account. {% if paidLayer.live %}A paper with a padlock opens with the <a href="/pass/">All Access pass</a>.{% else %}A paper with a padlock needs a free login to open.{% endif %} <a href="/exams/net/">Back to NET preparation</a></p>
</section>

{% set hubLinksText = "Pages that help you prepare for UGC-NET English." %}{% include "hub-links.njk" %}
<script src="/assets/net-pyq-live.js" defer></script>
